{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-09T20:36:41.776Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary:\n\n**Changed**\n- **`src/cli/mcp-protocol.ts`** (new, 201 lines): `createMcpHandler(tools, info)` exporting `McpTool`, `McpToolResult`, `McpServerInfo` (plus `McpHandler`/`McpAnswer`). It answers one parsed JSON-RPC 2.0 message with the full `{ jsonrpc: '2.0', id, result | error }` envelope, serves both protocol eras with no SDK, no imports at all, and never rejects. Modern requests are validated before the method runs (`2026-07-28` + `clientCapabilities`), get `resultType: 'complete'` first and the `serverInfo` `_meta`; legacy results carry neither. Ready for the task's config: `pnpm verify` exits 0 — all 3618+137 preexisting tests pass unchanged, typechecks, build, and lint green.\n- **`tests/mcp-protocol.test.ts`** (new): builds the handler with nine stub tools named as in \"MCP planning tools\" (`plan` throws), and asserts every row of the \"Requests and answers\" table plus \"A throwing tool\" with exact `assert.deepEqual` on the whole answer, a `result`-without-`method` → null case, and a never-rejects property check. 15 tests, all passing; biome-clean.\n- `createMcpHandler` carries `@scenario cli-foundation: Requests and answers`, `@scenario cli-foundation: A throwing tool`, `@adr 014`.\n\n**Verification**: the task's verify command passes (15/15), and the proposal's `pnpm verify` passes end to end. Result file written to `.run/results/1.md`; no other files touched."}}
