{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T00:33:57.153Z","data":{"text":"Task 1 complete. Summary:\n\n**Implemented `src/cli/mcp-protocol.ts`** (223 lines, no imports, no I/O):\n- Exports `createMcpHandler(tools, info)`, `McpTool`, `McpToolResult`, `McpServerInfo` (plus `McpAnswer`).\n- Serves both eras: legacy `initialize`/`ping`/`tools/list`/`tools/call`, modern `server/discover` with `_meta` validation.\n- Modern requests checked before dispatch: `-32022` for unsupported version, `-32602` for missing `clientCapabilities`; modern results get `resultType: 'complete'` and `_meta` server info, legacy results don't.\n- No `method` or no `id` → null; unknown tool → `-32602`; unknown method → `-32601`; tool throw → `Error: <message>\\n` with `isError: true`; handler never rejects.\n- Tagged `@scenario cli-foundation: Requests and answers`, `@scenario cli-foundation: A throwing tool`, `@adr 014`.\n\n**Added `tests/mcp-protocol.test.ts`** covering every \"Requests and answers\" row with exact `assert.deepEqual`, the throwing tool, a successful call, and the no-method null case.\n\n**Verification:** task verify passes (14/14), and `pnpm verify` passes (typechecks, build, full test suite, lint).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/163-local-mcp/.run/results/1.md`."}}
